  "notes": [
    "Ids are random per run, so meta.options uses strategy similarity: ids are declared meaningless, matches carry no rekey facet, and a matched pair that differs only by its id is unchanged (13 of the 37 matches). Union ids are the run-B ids for matched and added nodes and the run-A ids for removed nodes.",
    "Every match below scores ≥ 0.85 on label, types and attributes alone (aliases make most label variants exact); none relies on neighbour propagation.",
    "pitchblende ↔ uraninite (pitchblende) is deliberately ambiguous (pitchblende is a variety of uraninite): label similarity ≈ 0.69 with equal type and formula gives ≈ 0.77 before and ≈ 0.70 after neighbour evidence, so it stays a below-threshold suggestion and the two nodes are reported as removed / added. Their statements follow suit: radium –extracted_from→ is a target-end retarget (radium exists in both runs), while pitchblende –mined_in→ Jáchymov and uraninite –mined_in→ Jáchymov are a removed plus an added edge, because a source-end retarget requires both subjects to exist in both versions (docs/algorithms.md §5).",
    "Albert Einstein (and its collaborated_with edge) is a hallucination of run A; Gustave Bémont and the French Academy of Sciences appear only in run B."
  ],
